\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\section{Introduction}
Solid-state batteries promise \textbf{higher energy density} than conventional cells.
\section{Methods}
We synthesize three electrolytes and measure ionic conductivity. The \textbf{key observation} is that annealing doubles grain size. We also report \textbf{cycling stability} over 200 cycles.
\section{Conclusion}
Our results highlight \textbf{a viable route} to practical solid electrolytes.
